      "content": "\"A moderate contraction\" and \"measured pullback\" definitely sound a lot smoother. \n\nI'm thinking of trying to combine that with the \"optimization\" idea we discussed earlier to create a really cohesive narrative. If I can write a summary that makes the 8% look like a very small, intentional part of our broader strategy, I think I can get through this meeting unscathed.\n\nCan you go ahead and draft the full performance summary for me? Please use that \"tactical recalibration\" angle and integrate the idea of a \"moderate contraction\" or \"measured pullback\" to describe the magnitude. I want the final version to be a polished, professional piece that effectively makes the 8% feel like a minor, controlled, and expected event so I can keep the clients' confidence intact.",
